{"type":"message","id":"aa06d272","parentId":"f76a154b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T23:01:27.521Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The /send endpoint keeps returning 401 Unauthorized for POST requests. But the health endpoint works, and the /history endpoint works. \n\nThe problem might be that the `Content-Length` header is being sent incorrectly due to the JSON body format, or there's an issue with how Cloudflare Workers is handling the POST body.\n\nLet me try a simpler approach with --data-raw and see if that helps. Actually, let me try without JSON encoding issues.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-8dcb74b7-e976-471a-a292-4d1570d32f67","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  --data-raw 'content=[Heartbeat 23:00 UTC] 761min | 96nodes | S0 761min | 349+ milestones&type=message' 2>&1"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"curl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-raw 'content=[Heartbeat 23:00 UTC] 761min | 96nodes | S0 761min | 349+ milestones&type=message' 2>&1\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":195,"output":206,"cacheRead":19168,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19569,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779404482600,"responseId":"chatcmpl-18f0ee94-0390-4a35-8860-7b18a44a0129"}}
