{"type":"message","id":"45d38eee","parentId":"f05832a0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T23:01:31.080Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send is returning error code 1101, which seems to be a Cloudflare Workers specific error. The health endpoint works fine, and GET /history also works, but POST /send consistently returns 1101. This appears to be a service-side issue with the send endpoint, not an authentication issue (we get 401 for wrong auth but 1101 for the POST even with correct auth header format).\n\nLet me try different approaches:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-649ab872-a434-439c-81ff-c9a976745888","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check what error code 1101 is in Cloudflare Workers context - try without body encoding issues\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  --data-raw '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"# Check what error code 1101 is in Cloudflare Workers context - try without body encoding issues\\ncurl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  --data-raw '{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"test\\\"}' 2>&1\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":137,"output":210,"cacheRead":19360,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19707,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779404487691,"responseId":"chatcmpl-bb041e4e-adbf-40c1-905d-42994c0619c2"}}
